1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,020
Restaurant steaks cost a fortune, and
cooking one

2
00:00:03,030 --> 00:00:05,142
at home can go wrong in a hurry,

3
00:00:05,317 --> 00:00:07,789
with grey meat and a smoky kitchen.

4
00:00:08,452 --> 00:00:10,938
But in seven simple steps, you can cook

5
00:00:10,948 --> 00:00:13,341
a juicy steak with a deep brown crust

6
00:00:13,351 --> 00:00:16,648
in a regular pan, in about fifteen
minutes.

7
00:00:17,194 --> 00:00:19,982
No special equipment is required, apart
from a

8
00:00:19,992 --> 00:00:22,165
good pan, and I'll show you how to

9
00:00:22,175 --> 00:00:24,345
fix the most common problems.

10
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,016
WikiTube.

11
00:00:26,191 --> 00:00:28,454
Whatever it is, here's how.

12
00:00:28,733 --> 00:00:31,344
A great steak depends on three things.

13
00:00:31,577 --> 00:00:34,586
A dry surface, a very hot pan, and

14
00:00:34,596 --> 00:00:36,278
a short rest at the end.

15
00:00:36,569 --> 00:00:37,427
That's it.

16
00:00:37,603 --> 00:00:40,133
You don't need a grill, a special cut

17
00:00:40,226 --> 00:00:41,781
or a fancy sauce.

18
00:00:42,932 --> 00:00:45,917
We'll use a thick steak, salt, a little

19
00:00:45,927 --> 00:00:47,679
oil and a skillet.

20
00:00:48,226 --> 00:00:51,281
Once you understand why each step matters,
you

21
00:00:51,291 --> 00:00:54,935
can repeat this result every time, with
ribeye,

22
00:00:55,110 --> 00:00:59,394
sirloin, strip steak or whichever cut you
prefer.

23
00:01:00,358 --> 00:01:02,984
Don't be afraid of high heat, because that

24
00:01:02,994 --> 00:01:04,351
is what makes the difference.

25
00:01:04,805 --> 00:01:07,567
Open a window, and let's begin.

26
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:09,351
Here's what you need.

27
00:01:09,805 --> 00:01:12,337
A steak at least one inch, or two

28
00:01:12,347 --> 00:01:14,634
and a half centimetres, thick.

29
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:17,907
Coarse salt and black pepper.

30
00:01:18,268 --> 00:01:22,458
A heavy skillet, ideally cast iron or
stainless steel.

31
00:01:22,819 --> 00:01:25,268
A neutral oil with a high smoke point.

32
00:01:25,559 --> 00:01:28,635
Butter, garlic and thyme if you like.

33
00:01:28,996 --> 00:01:31,679
And a meat thermometer, which is the best

34
00:01:31,689 --> 00:01:34,846
tool for getting perfect results every
time.

35
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,328
Step one.

36
00:01:36,782 --> 00:01:38,711
Choose a steak that is at least one

37
00:01:38,721 --> 00:01:43,004
inch thick, because thin steaks overcook
before they brown.

38
00:01:43,968 --> 00:01:47,462
Ribeye, strip and sirloin are all
excellent.

39
00:01:47,915 --> 00:01:49,624
Take the meat out of the fridge about

40
00:01:49,634 --> 00:01:52,747
thirty minutes before cooking, so the
chill comes

41
00:01:52,757 --> 00:01:53,882
off the surface.

42
00:01:54,429 --> 00:01:57,484
Then pat it completely dry with paper
towels,

43
00:01:57,494 --> 00:01:58,863
on every side.

44
00:01:59,827 --> 00:02:01,675
This is the most important part of this

45
00:02:01,685 --> 00:02:04,252
step, because water on the meat turns to

46
00:02:04,262 --> 00:02:07,155
steam in the pan, and steamed meat turns

47
00:02:07,165 --> 00:02:08,975
grey instead of brown.

48
00:02:09,638 --> 00:02:12,121
A dry steak browns in minutes.

49
00:02:12,575 --> 00:02:15,491
Thicker cuts forgive small timing errors,
which is

50
00:02:15,501 --> 00:02:17,160
ideal when you're learning.

51
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:18,825
Step two.

52
00:02:19,116 --> 00:02:22,520
Season the steak on all sides, including
the

53
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:26,905
edges, with coarse salt and freshly ground
black pepper.

54
00:02:27,707 --> 00:02:30,623
Be generous, since much of the seasoning
falls

55
00:02:30,633 --> 00:02:33,375
off in the pan, and a thick steak

56
00:02:33,385 --> 00:02:35,404
needs more salt than you think.

57
00:02:36,206 --> 00:02:38,855
For the best flavor, salt it as soon

58
00:02:38,865 --> 00:02:40,524
as you take it out of the fridge,

59
00:02:40,583 --> 00:02:43,310
so the salt has half an hour to be
absorbed.

60
00:02:43,973 --> 00:02:45,902
If you are in a rush, salt it

61
00:02:45,912 --> 00:02:47,571
just before it hits the pan.

62
00:02:47,932 --> 00:02:51,265
Avoid salting and then waiting five
minutes, because

63
00:02:51,275 --> 00:02:54,607
that draws out moisture and leaves the
surface wet.

64
00:02:55,571 --> 00:02:58,949
Press the seasoning gently into the meat
so it sticks.

65
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:00,707
Step three.

66
00:03:01,161 --> 00:03:04,158
Place a heavy skillet over medium-high to
high

67
00:03:04,168 --> 00:03:06,654
heat and let it heat for three to

68
00:03:06,664 --> 00:03:09,531
five minutes, until it is really hot.

69
00:03:09,984 --> 00:03:12,331
Add a tablespoon of oil with a high

70
00:03:12,341 --> 00:03:16,880
smoke point, like avocado, canola or
sunflower,

71
00:03:17,055 --> 00:03:20,711
and wait until it shimmers and just starts
to smoke.

72
00:03:21,513 --> 00:03:23,976
A hot pan is what creates the brown

73
00:03:23,986 --> 00:03:27,306
crust, which is where most of the flavor
lives.

74
00:03:27,667 --> 00:03:29,584
Don't use olive oil or butter at this

75
00:03:29,594 --> 00:03:32,298
point, because they burn too fast.

76
00:03:32,845 --> 00:03:36,106
Turn on your extractor fan and open a
window.

77
00:03:36,653 --> 00:03:39,325
If your pan smokes heavily, lower the heat

78
00:03:39,335 --> 00:03:41,865
slightly rather than starting again.

79
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,479
Step four.

80
00:03:44,142 --> 00:03:46,605
Lay the steak in the pan, away from

81
00:03:46,615 --> 00:03:49,447
you, so the oil doesn't splash toward you.

82
00:03:49,807 --> 00:03:52,488
It should sizzle loudly right away.

83
00:03:53,151 --> 00:03:54,892
Now leave it alone.

84
00:03:55,694 --> 00:03:58,409
Don't poke, press or slide it.

85
00:03:59,211 --> 00:04:02,034
For a one inch steak, sear for about

86
00:04:02,044 --> 00:04:04,902
two to three minutes, until a deep brown

87
00:04:04,912 --> 00:04:07,445
crust forms and the meat releases from the

88
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:08,847
pan on its own.

89
00:04:09,393 --> 00:04:12,109
If it sticks, it isn't ready to turn.

90
00:04:12,772 --> 00:04:15,351
Use tongs to sear the fatty edge for

91
00:04:15,361 --> 00:04:16,858
thirty seconds too.

92
00:04:17,404 --> 00:04:20,123
Resist the urge to flip it early, because

93
00:04:20,133 --> 00:04:22,198
patience builds the crust.

94
00:04:23,349 --> 00:04:26,357
The sound tells you everything, so listen
for

95
00:04:26,367 --> 00:04:28,944
a steady, strong sizzle.

96
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:30,579
Step five.

97
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:33,658
Turn the steak over with tongs, and lower

98
00:04:33,668 --> 00:04:35,095
the heat to medium.

99
00:04:36,246 --> 00:04:38,917
Add a tablespoon or two of butter, a

100
00:04:38,927 --> 00:04:42,131
few crushed garlic cloves and a sprig of
thyme.

101
00:04:43,281 --> 00:04:45,941
When the butter foams, tilt the pan
slightly

102
00:04:45,951 --> 00:04:48,147
and spoon the melted butter over the steak

103
00:04:48,157 --> 00:04:50,536
again and again for about a minute.

104
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:54,205
Basting adds flavor and cooks the top
gently.

105
00:04:55,356 --> 00:04:57,505
Cook the second side for another two to

106
00:04:57,515 --> 00:05:00,010
three minutes, depending on thickness.

107
00:05:00,975 --> 00:05:03,299
Keep the heat moderate so the butter turns

108
00:05:03,309 --> 00:05:06,535
nutty and golden, not burnt and bitter.

109
00:05:07,198 --> 00:05:09,568
If your steak is very thick, finish it

110
00:05:09,578 --> 00:05:12,389
in a hot oven, at around 200 degrees

111
00:05:12,399 --> 00:05:17,298
Celsius or 400 Fahrenheit, for a few
minutes.

112
00:05:17,833 --> 00:05:18,947
Step six.

113
00:05:19,238 --> 00:05:22,282
The most reliable way to judge doneness is

114
00:05:22,292 --> 00:05:25,367
a thermometer pushed into the thickest
part of the steak.

115
00:05:25,821 --> 00:05:28,040
Remove the steak from the pan at about

116
00:05:28,050 --> 00:05:32,322
125 degrees Fahrenheit, or 52 Celsius,

117
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:37,131
for rare, 130 to 135, or 54

118
00:05:37,141 --> 00:05:41,691
to 57 Celsius, for medium-rare, and 140,

119
00:05:41,785 --> 00:05:44,942
or 60 Celsius, for medium.

120
00:05:45,604 --> 00:05:48,912
The temperature rises a few degrees while
it rests.

121
00:05:49,877 --> 00:05:54,415
Food safety agencies advise 145 degrees
Fahrenheit,

122
00:05:54,590 --> 00:05:58,246
or 63 Celsius, for whole cuts of beef,

123
00:05:58,607 --> 00:06:01,451
so choose the doneness that you are
comfortable with.

124
00:06:02,253 --> 00:06:04,797
Insert the probe from the side, and avoid

125
00:06:04,807 --> 00:06:06,838
touching bone or the pan.

126
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,537
Step seven.

127
00:06:09,502 --> 00:06:11,465
Move the steak to a board or a

128
00:06:11,475 --> 00:06:13,892
warm plate and let it rest for at

129
00:06:13,902 --> 00:06:16,829
least five minutes, and up to ten for

130
00:06:16,839 --> 00:06:18,406
a very thick cut.

131
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:22,527
During cooking, the juices are pushed to
the center.

132
00:06:23,074 --> 00:06:25,952
Resting lets them spread back through the
meat,

133
00:06:26,127 --> 00:06:28,184
so they stay in the steak instead of

134
00:06:28,194 --> 00:06:29,586
running onto the board.

135
00:06:30,551 --> 00:06:32,619
Then look for the direction of the muscle

136
00:06:32,629 --> 00:06:36,076
fibres, the grain, and slice across it.

137
00:06:37,227 --> 00:06:39,919
Short fibres feel more tender in your
mouth.

138
00:06:40,466 --> 00:06:44,331
Spoon the pan butter over the slices and
serve immediately.

139
00:06:44,867 --> 00:06:47,330
If your steak turned grey, the pan was

140
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:49,699
not hot enough, or you cooked too much

141
00:06:49,709 --> 00:06:50,799
meat at once.

142
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:53,435
Cook one or two steaks at a time.

143
00:06:53,889 --> 00:06:56,421
If the kitchen fills with smoke, switch on

144
00:06:56,431 --> 00:06:58,639
the fan and check that your oil has

145
00:06:58,649 --> 00:06:59,890
a high smoke point.

146
00:07:00,251 --> 00:07:03,361
Add the butter late, because it burns
quickly.

147
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:07,150
For a very thick steak, try a reverse
sear.

148
00:07:07,696 --> 00:07:10,043
Cook it first in a low oven, around

149
00:07:10,053 --> 00:07:15,024
250 degrees Fahrenheit or 120 Celsius,

150
00:07:15,034 --> 00:07:18,899
until it is about fifteen degrees below
your target temperature.

151
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:22,916
Then sear it in a very hot pan.

152
00:07:23,463 --> 00:07:25,937
After resting, add a splash of stock to

153
00:07:25,947 --> 00:07:27,827
the pan for a quick sauce.

154
00:07:28,367 --> 00:07:30,725
Put leftover steak in a covered container
in

155
00:07:30,735 --> 00:07:33,210
the fridge within two hours, and eat it

156
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:35,030
within three to four days.

157
00:07:35,263 --> 00:07:39,465
Cold sliced steak is wonderful in salads
and sandwiches.

158
00:07:39,756 --> 00:07:41,894
To reheat it, use a low oven or

159
00:07:41,904 --> 00:07:43,902
a pan with a little butter, so it

160
00:07:43,912 --> 00:07:45,374
does not turn tough.

161
00:07:46,525 --> 00:07:49,229
Make it steaming hot all the way through.

162
00:07:49,767 --> 00:07:52,958
Here are the three mistakes that ruin most
steaks.

163
00:07:53,505 --> 00:07:57,243
First, a wet steak and a lukewarm pan.

164
00:07:57,603 --> 00:08:00,702
This steams the meat, and it turns grey.

165
00:08:01,852 --> 00:08:04,754
Dry it, and heat the pan properly.

166
00:08:05,904 --> 00:08:08,272
Second, moving the steak around.

167
00:08:08,726 --> 00:08:10,771
Every time you lift it, you lose the

168
00:08:10,781 --> 00:08:12,359
crust that is forming.

169
00:08:12,719 --> 00:08:15,447
And third, slicing straight away.

170
00:08:16,109 --> 00:08:18,500
The juices need a few minutes to settle,

171
00:08:18,594 --> 00:08:20,940
otherwise they pour out on the board and

172
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,679
the steak tastes dry.

173
00:08:23,226 --> 00:08:26,336
Avoid these three, and you'll get great
steak.

174
00:08:27,487 --> 00:08:30,298
Practice makes this easy, and the second
steak

175
00:08:30,308 --> 00:08:32,501
is always better than the first.

176
00:08:33,067 --> 00:08:34,169
Let's recap.

177
00:08:34,832 --> 00:08:37,373
Pick a thick steak and pat it dry.

178
00:08:38,338 --> 00:08:40,380
Season generously with salt.

179
00:08:41,531 --> 00:08:43,306
Get the pan very hot.

180
00:08:44,456 --> 00:08:46,139
Sear without moving it.

181
00:08:47,289 --> 00:08:51,967
Flip, add butter, garlic and thyme, and
baste.

182
00:08:52,630 --> 00:08:54,614
Check the temperature with a thermometer.

183
00:08:55,068 --> 00:08:58,306
And rest the steak, then slice across the
grain.

184
00:08:58,969 --> 00:09:03,960
The bonus sections cover fixes, a reverse
sear and leftovers.

185
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:07,239
That's how you cook a steak perfectly in a
pan.

186
00:09:07,599 --> 00:09:11,139
If dinner just got better, subscribe to
WikiTube,

187
00:09:11,372 --> 00:09:14,901
because we publish a new how-to every
single day.

188
00:09:15,261 --> 00:09:16,970
Tell us in the comments how you like

189
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:19,048
your steak cooked, and what you would like

190
00:09:19,058 --> 00:09:20,601
us to explain next.

191
00:09:21,751 --> 00:09:22,993
See you tomorrow.

192
